      "node_id": "kg_doc_5",
      "node_type": "kg",
      "content": "Major General Robert Walker Grow (February 14, 1895 – November 3, 1985) was a senior United States Army officer who commanded the 6th Armored Division during World War II. He was notable for his court martial in 1951 for failing to safeguard classified information.",
      "depth": 0,
      "parent_id": null,
      "value": 0.99999999366133,
